    "abstract": "FlashAttention is an IO-aware exact attention algorithm that uses tiling to reduce reads and writes between GPU high-bandwidth memory and on-chip SRAM. It requires fewer HBM accesses than standard attention and is optimal for a range of SRAM sizes. It yields 15% end-to-end speed-up on BERT-large, 3x on GPT-2, 2.4x on Long Range Arena, and enables the first better-than-chance results on Path-X and Path-256.",
    "domain": "NLP",
    "key_claims": [
      "Tiling with an online softmax plus recomputation in the backward pass computes exact attention without materialising the N x N matrix.",
      "FlashAttention requires Theta(N^2 d^2 / M) HBM accesses versus Theta(N d + N^2) for standard attention, and this is optimal for a range of M.",
      "End-to-end speed-ups: 15% on BERT-large (seq 512), 3x on GPT-2 (seq 1K), 2.4x on Long Range Arena.",
      "Longer context enables 61.4% on Path-X (16K) and 63.1% on Path-256 (64K), the first better-than-chance results.",
      "Block-sparse FlashAttention is faster still, with IO complexity reduced proportionally to sparsity."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
